<div class="pa-callout pa-callout--warning mb-4 sheet-demo-notice">
    <span class="pa-callout__icon"><span class="pa-icon pa-icon--warning" aria-hidden="true"></span></span>
    <div class="pa-callout__content">
        <h4 class="pa-callout__heading">Semi-experimental</h4>
        <p><code>pa-sheet</code> and the form primitives shown here (<code>pc-grid</code>, <code>pa-table--plain</code>, the print colour modes, and the rotation / vertical-text utilities) are still stabilising. <strong>Class names, modifiers and markup shape may change</strong> in upcoming releases — pin an exact version if you build on them, and check the CHANGELOG before upgrading.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<p class="sheet-demo-intro">Printable <strong>paper documents</strong> — invoices, orders, quotes, receipts and payment reminders — built from a set of blocks instead of hand-rolled HTML. <code>pa-sheet</code> is the white, centred, A4-width page with a screen-only drop shadow and a built-in <code>@media&nbsp;print</code> layer. Line items reuse the ordinary <code>pa-table</code>; label/value metadata reuse <code>pa-fields</code> / <code>pa-desc-table</code>. The examples below use fictional data (Twin Peaks Ltd. &amp; friends).</p>

<div class="mb-8 sheet-demo-controls">
    <button type="button" class="pa-btn pa-btn--primary" onclick="window.print()">
        {{> partials/printer-icon}} Print whole page
    </button>
    <span class="pa-text pa-text--secondary ms-2"><code>window.print()</code> prints the entire document. Each sheet below also has its own button that prints <strong>just that one sheet</strong> in isolation via <code>pureAdmin.printElement()</code> — no page-level print CSS needed.</span>

    <!-- Print colour policy — three direct-print buttons. The policy lives
         inside @media print (invisible on screen), so each button prints the
         invoice above in one mode straight into the print preview. It briefly
         adds the modifier class to #sheet-invoice; printElement() clones the
         element synchronously, so the class is captured and removed again with
         no on-screen flicker. Most visible on a dark theme (e.g. Cobalt2). -->
    <div class="mt-3" style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <span class="pa-text pa-text--secondary"><strong>Test print colour modes</strong> — opens a print preview of the invoice below:</span>
        <div role="group" aria-label="Print colour modes" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 0.5rem;">
            <button type="button" class="pa-btn pa-btn--sm pa-btn--primary" onclick="printInvoiceMode('', 'Invoice — ink on paper')">Ink on paper (default)</button>
            <button type="button" class="pa-btn pa-btn--sm pa-btn--secondary" onclick="printInvoiceMode('pa-sheet--print-color', 'Invoice — theme colours')">Theme colours</button>
            <button type="button" class="pa-btn pa-btn--sm pa-btn--secondary" onclick="printInvoiceMode('pa-sheet--print-grayscale', 'Invoice — greyscale')">Greyscale</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-1">
        <span class="pa-text pa-text--secondary">All three print on white paper (never a toner-heavy background). Switch to a dark theme (e.g. Cobalt2) to feel the difference: <strong>Ink on paper</strong> is pure black-and-white; <strong>Theme colours</strong> keeps the accent/brand colours (coloured title, logo) on white; <strong>Greyscale</strong> desaturates those to grey.</span>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Hide the demo chrome when printing so only the sheets land on paper. -->
<style>
@media print {
    /* Hide app chrome + demo-only scaffolding so only the sheets print.
       (Transient overlays — settings panel, profile panel, toasts, command
       palette — are hidden by core's own @media print rules as of 3.3.0-rc03.) */
    .pc-sidebar, .pc-navbar, .pc-app-header, .pc-page-header, .pc-footer,
    .sheet-demo-controls, .sheet-demo-intro, .sheet-demo-reference, .sheet-demo-notice { display: none !important; }
    .pc-main, .pc-content, .pc-layout__main { margin: 0 !important; padding: 0 !important; }

    /* The app's main scroll region keeps a themed (accent-coloured) scrollbar
       when it overflows; drop the scroll so no scrollbar paints on paper. */
    .pc-layout__content { overflow: visible !important; }

    /* pa-sheet--fill pins its footer position:fixed so it sits at the bottom of
       a SINGLE isolated sheet. On a whole-page print (several sheets + this
       page's own content) a fixed footer would repeat on every page and overlay
       everything after it. Un-pin it — but ONLY for the live page, NOT the
       printElement() iframe, whose <html data-pa-print> must keep the intended
       single-sheet pinned-footer behaviour. */
    html:not([data-pa-print]) .pa-sheet--fill > :last-child { position: static !important; }
}
</style>


<!-- ============================================================
     EXAMPLE 1 — Standard tax invoice (gridded / boxed style)
     ============================================================ -->
<div id="sheet-invoice" class="pa-sheet pa-sheet--framed mb-8">
